19:<p>VoiceReminder is built and run by an independent developer ("we", "us", "our"), who is the data controller for everything described here. There's no support department to get lost in &mdash; questions come straight to a person, at <a href="mailto:athea.hab@gmail.com">athea.hab@gmail.com</a>.</p>
21:<h2>2. What we collect</h2>
22:<p>VoiceReminder has no accounts and no sign-in. We never ask for your name, email address, phone number, or contacts, and we don't collect your location. Here is everything the app actually handles:</p>
27:  <li><strong>An install identifier.</strong> A random string your device generates the first time you open the app. It is not your Apple Account, not a hardware serial number, and not tied to your identity. It exists so our backend can tell your reminders apart from everyone else's. Delete the app and it's gone; reinstall and a brand-new one is made.</li>
28:  <li><strong>Crash and diagnostic reports.</strong> If something breaks, technical details &mdash; device model, operating system version, and where in the code the failure happened &mdash; go to our error-monitoring service so we can fix it.</li>
42:<p>Because that work happens off your phone, the app asks for your explicit permission before your first recording and won't record until you agree. You stay in charge of it: you can stop at any time by turning off microphone access for VoiceReminder in your device's <strong>Settings</strong> &mdash; nothing further is recorded or processed from that moment, and reminders you've already made keep working. You can also skip voice entirely and type reminders by hand.</p>
46:  <li><strong>Your consent</strong> &mdash; for processing your voice recordings as described in section 3. Freely given, and revocable at any time by turning off microphone access in your device's Settings.</li>
52:<p><strong>We do not sell your personal data.</strong> We never share it for advertising, and nobody receives it for their own use &mdash; not to train their models, not to build profiles, not for anything of theirs.</p>
53:<p>Like nearly every app, VoiceReminder is delivered with the help of a small number of trusted providers. Each of them processes data on our behalf and on our instructions, and only for the one job it does for us:</p>
58:  <li><strong>Hosting and storage</strong> &mdash; to keep your reminders and their audio available to your device.</li>
62:<p>Each one sees only what its own job requires, is contractually bound to protect it, and is prohibited from using it for any purpose of its own. We pass on the smallest amount of data that lets each step work, and nothing beyond it.</p>
64:<p>Some of these providers operate outside the country you live in. Where that means a transfer out of the UK or EEA, we only work with providers that keep recognised safeguards in place for it &mdash; standard contractual clauses approved by the European Commission, or an equivalent protection. We may also disclose data where the law genuinely requires it.</p>
70:  <li><strong>Reminders on your device:</strong> stored locally so the app works offline, and removed when you delete the reminder or uninstall the app.</li>
71:  <li><strong>Crash reports:</strong> retained by our error-monitoring service for a limited period (typically up to 90 days) and then discarded.</li>
77:  <li>We don't sell or rent your data to anyone.</li>
79:  <li>We don't collect your location, contacts, photos, or health records.</li>
81:  <li>We don't let anyone else use your data for their own purposes &mdash; the providers that help run the app work for us, under contract, and that's the whole relationship.</li>
85:<h2>8. How we keep your data safe</h2>
86:<p>Everything travels over encrypted (HTTPS) connections and is stored by our backend provider on encrypted infrastructure. Reminders are scoped to the install identifier that created them, so one device can't read another's. In the App Store version of the app, diagnostic reporting is limited to crashes and errors: it doesn't send app logs, screenshots, or the contents of your screen. No system is perfectly secure, but we keep the amount of data we hold deliberately small &mdash; the less there is, the less there is to lose.</p>
91:  <li><strong>Access</strong> the data we hold about you, and get a copy of it.</li>
93:  <li><strong>Delete</strong> your data &mdash; the "right to be forgotten".</li>
97:  <li><strong>Complain</strong> to your local data protection authority if you think we've got it wrong.</li>
101:<p>Most of it you can do yourself, instantly: delete a reminder in the app and its text and audio are deleted from our backend too, and turning off microphone access for VoiceReminder in your device's Settings stops any further voice processing.</p>
103:  <p>For anything else &mdash; a copy of your data, or deletion of everything associated with your install &mdash; email <a href="mailto:athea.hab@gmail.com">athea.hab@gmail.com</a> and say what you'd like. Because the app has no accounts, we can't look you up by name or email, so please include enough detail to identify your records (for example the titles and times of a few of your reminders); we may ask a follow-up question before acting. We'll respond within 30 days, free of charge.</p>
108:<p>VoiceReminder is not directed at children under 13, and we don't knowingly collect data from them. If you believe a child has used the app and sent us data, email us and we'll delete it.</p>
111:<p>If we change how the app handles data, we'll update this page and change the "last updated" date at the top. Material changes &mdash; a new category of data, or a new kind of provider &mdash; will also be surfaced in the app. Continuing to use VoiceReminder after a change means you accept the updated policy.</p>
